{
  "name": "leaf-beetle",
  "_about": "The rosemary beetle (Chrysolina americana), 8 mm long: a convex oval, flat below, metallic green striped lengthwise with purple-red; a broad metallic pronotum, a small head, short antennae thickening to the tip, short metallic legs. Coats: the dock leaf beetle (Gastrophysa viridula, plain metallic green) and the red poplar leaf beetle (Chrysomela populi: red wing cases, a blue-black front). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
